From: Stamp-P4 maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] char/mem: keep /dev/mem mmap working on NOMMU under
 mmap_prepare

Linux 7.2 converted /dev/mem to f_op->mmap_prepare, which ends with
mmap_action_remap_full().  The NOMMU mmap_action backend (mm/util.c)
rejects every action but MMAP_NOTHING with WARN_ONCE and -EINVAL, so
every /dev/mem mmap on NOMMU now fails (devmem, boot-shim PSRAM
staging, ES_DWC2_STATUS all EINVAL).

With NOMMU_MAP_DIRECT, get_unmapped_area_mem() already places the VMA
at the physical address, so no remap is needed.  Skip the action on
NOMMU and do what the NOMMU remap_pfn_range() did instead: verify the
direct placement and set the I/O VMA flags that the compat path
copies back into the VMA.

No upstream fix exists as of 7.2.11 (checked torvalds/master).

---
diff --git a/drivers/char/mem.c b/drivers/char/mem.c
index 63253d1de5d7..a2fca41f4558 100644
--- a/drivers/char/mem.c
+++ b/drivers/char/mem.c
@@ -355,9 +355,23 @@
 
 	desc->vm_ops = &mmap_mem_ops;
 
+#ifndef CONFIG_MMU
+	/*
+	 * NOMMU's mmap_action machinery rejects everything but
+	 * MMAP_NOTHING, so we must not request a remap here.  None is
+	 * needed: with NOMMU_MAP_DIRECT, get_unmapped_area_mem() already
+	 * placed the VMA at the physical address.  Do what the NOMMU
+	 * remap_pfn_range() used to do instead.
+	 */
+	if (desc->start != (unsigned long)offset)
+		return -EINVAL;
+	vma_desc_set_flags(desc, VMA_IO_BIT, VMA_PFNMAP_BIT,
+			 VMA_DONTEXPAND_BIT, VMA_DONTDUMP_BIT);
+#else
 	/* Remap-pfn-range will mark the range with the I/O flag. */
 	mmap_action_remap_full(desc, desc->pgoff);
 	desc->action.error_override = -EAGAIN;
+#endif
 
 	return 0;
 }
